# Build output
bin/
obj/
*.user
artifacts/

# Local test data captured from the reference server
traces/
*.trace
*.gg2trace

# ...except the recordings the tests are built on. Those are oracles, not
# scratch data: WeaponBlockTests and PhysicsParityTests assert they exist, so
# without this a fresh clone fails two tests that pass on the machine that
# recorded them. docs/PARITY.md says parity fixtures live with the tests and
# run in CI; this is what makes that true.
!tests/GG2.Tests/Fixtures/*.trace

# Claude Code session automation: the hooks, settings.json and commands that
# carry a handoff from one session to the next.
#
# ⚠️ The negation is load-bearing. ~/.gitignore_global excludes .claude/
# wholesale, and git will not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY to find a
# negated file inside it - so the directory has to be re-included first or
# .claude/hooks/ is silently untracked and a fresh clone gets none of it.
!.claude/

# ...but handoffs stay out. They are disposable messages to the next session,
# not documentation. See CLAUDE.md, "Where documentation goes".
.claude/notes/

# Machine-specific overrides, never team config.
.claude/settings.local.json

# The bot nav graphs at nav/ are CHECKED IN as of 2026-09-01, deliberately.
#
# They are gg2-nav-gen's output rather than this repo's source, which is the
# usual argument for ignoring them -- and it loses to the fact that without them
# a clone cannot run a bot, and regenerating them needs a Game Maker 8 build of
# a fork that most people cloning this will never have. A generated artefact
# whose generator is not reproducible from this repository is, in practice, a
# source file.
#
# 34 MB on disk and ~1.2 MB packed: hex text compresses about 28:1, so the
# objection that they would bloat the repository was measured and is wrong.
#
# They used to be read out of the reference tree's GM8 build directory, which
# coupled the test suite to one particular checkout of a fork.
# ReferenceTree.NavCacheDirectory looks at nav/, or at GG2_NAVCACHE.
TestResults/

# Fleet analytics collected by scripts/fleet-analytics.sh. Player names; never commit.
deploy/analytics/

# scripts/ is the OPERATOR's tooling, not the project's: the fleet deploy, the
# Linux/Windows build wrappers, the fleet-state and analytics readers, and the
# one-line admin-panel tunnels. It is specific to the three hosts this
# repository's author personally runs, so it was untracked on 2026-09-15 and
# left on disk. Nothing secret was in it -- every password is read from the
# host's own gg2.ini and masked before it reaches a terminal -- so the history
# was deliberately NOT rewritten; the files are simply no longer carried.
#
# docs/DEPLOY.md, CONFIG.md, WEBADMIN.md and ANALYTICS.md still describe these
# scripts. That is on purpose: they document how the fleet is actually run, and
# the layout they describe is reproducible without them.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash: a bare `scripts/` matches a directory of that
# name at ANY depth, so a future src/Something/scripts/ would be ignored
# silently and nothing would go red.
/scripts/
